# SECTION 07 — ENGINEERING PERSPECTIVE

## Engineering Perspective

Engineering shall build capabilities as independent operational modules.

Capabilities become the primary engineering unit of the COREI Workbench.

---

## Capability Contract

Every capability shall publish a formal capability contract.

Minimum contract sections include:

* Capability Identity
* Institutional Responsibility
* Supported Operators
* Required Permissions
* Runtime Dependencies
* Commands
* Search Integration
* Context Integration
* AI Integration
* Events
* Extension Points
* Audit Requirements
* Performance Requirements
* Lifecycle

No capability enters the Workbench without a contract.

---

## Runtime Integration

Every capability shall integrate through Workbench services.

Capabilities consume:

* Context Service
* Search Service
* Command Service
* Notification Service
* Workspace Service
* History Service
* Permission Service
* Configuration Service

Capabilities shall never duplicate Workbench responsibilities.

---

## Capability Lifecycle

Every capability follows one governed lifecycle.

Registration

↓

Validation

↓

Dependency Resolution

↓

Initialization

↓

Activation

↓

Execution

↓

Monitoring

↓

